biome_metatiles:
Use case: stylized-concept
Asset type: Gaiden-scale WORLD MAP TERRAIN METATILE source atlas.
Reference 1: Fire Emblem Gaiden world map. Match how its forests form continuous dark masses and mountains form connected ridges, not a scatter of large individual trees or boulders. Reference 2: selected quiet B palette and modest flat pixel style. Keep subdued olive, ash gray/lilac, pearl-gray snow and gray-blue marsh. No neon green/gold from the original.
Exactly EIGHT fully separate complete WORLD terrain patches in a 4-column x 2-row transparent atlas. Each cell has wide transparent margin. Target 1536x768. No labels, gutters drawn, text, grid or scenery background.
These patches are conceived at 16x16-native tile density: complete patch widths about FOUR world tiles (64 native pixels), heights 2–4 tiles. Tiny conifer peaks and mountain crests within patches each about 6–12 native pixels, very coarse and economical, 2–3 tones per material. Each patch is a connected complete silhouette that can be divided along the native tile grid while preserving adjoining pixels. No realistic bark, pine needles, grass specks, faceted rock rendering, black high-contrast outline or diorama perspective.
Exact reading order:
Row1 Col1: complete irregular dense conifer forest mass, contiguous muted pine/olive tree canopies, dark connected shadow underneath, a stepped curved eastern forest boundary, roughly 4x3 tiles;
Row1 Col2: complete irregular dense round-canopy forest mass, connected olive foliage, broad calm canopy shapes, dark connected base, roughly 4x3 tiles;
Row1 Col3: long connected north-south mountain ridge bending slightly west in its lower part, a chain of tiny rounded mountain crests, gray-lilac shadow, connected broad bases, roughly 4x4 tiles;
Row1 Col4: long east-west connected mountain ridge, many small continuous mountain crests, 4x2 tiles, soft slate/lilac shade, not a line of separate pebble sprites.
Row2 Col1: complete contiguous conifer forest mass with pearl-gray snow caps, no white ground rectangle, 4x3 tiles;
Row2 Col2: complete winding connected mountain mass with modest snow crest strips, same tiny world-map mountain scale, 4x3 tiles;
Row2 Col3: complete long low moss-topped cliff edge with a quiet gray vertical front, a simple contiguous 4x1-tile strip;
Row2 Col4: low connected patch of olive reeds and a few shallow gray-blue pool pixels, irregular dark marsh footprint, 4x3 tiles, NO rectangular water or grass backdrop.
Classic near-vertical WORLD MAP representation like Gaiden: symbolic geography seen above, not a side-view object showcase and not close-up tactical scenery. All individual patches complete, separate and fully visible. Genuine transparent alpha around every silhouette, no white/blue/red fringe or checkerboard. Clear connected terrain patterns, tiny marks, quiet original fantasy game style.
